{"type": "run_started", "run_id": "939e49d8c789", "turn": 0, "step": 0, "seq": 1, "ts": 1792749008.325, "goal": "Design the node: an STM32G474 drives a DC motor with a 20 kHz PWM, talks UART at 115200 baud to an ESP32 and must stay under a 50 uA sleep-current budget. The system clock comes from the board's external crystal (HSE) through the PLL, at the highest SYSCLK the chip allows. Decompose the work into steps, work out the clock and PLL configuration, check the logic-level compatibility between the STM32G474 and the ESP32 and check the sleep-current budget. Give the design as a numbered plan with the numbers.", "project_id": "cli-e59c48", "ablations": [], "budgets": {"steps": 40, "tokens": 1500000, "usd": 0.5, "wall_s": 600.0, "ask_human": 3}}
